  - [1mUnit tests[0m — the store and model logic is pure and genuinely worth testing; the change-log invariant ("every state
    change has exactly one event") is a test, not a hope. Without a build step, the lightest option is Node's built-in
    [38;5;153mnode:test[39m runner, which needs no dependency at all.
  - [1mEnd-to-end tests[0m — Playwright against the real page. More setup; arguably premature for one screen.
  - [1mFuzz/property testing[0m — probably not worth it here.

  I'd set up the first two and skip the last two for now. E2E earns its keep once there are enough screens for a
  regression to hide in.
